WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.128
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:06.428 --> 00:00:09.745
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.045 --> 00:00:16.459
Unit fourteen: Consumer Behavior. Today you will use gradable adverbs and strong collocations.

4
00:00:16.759 --> 00:00:19.585
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:23.592
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.741
Purchase decision.

7
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.468
Purchase decision means the choice a customer makes about what to buy.

8
00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:33.814
Reviews strongly influence a purchase decision.

9
00:00:34.417 --> 00:00:37.162
Your turn. Say: Purchase decision.

10
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.210
Purchase decision.

11
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.357
Brand perception.

12
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:48.346
Brand perception means the ideas and feelings people have about a brand.

13
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.460
Brand perception improved after the recall.

14
00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.155
Your turn. Say: Brand perception.

15
00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.454
Brand perception.

16
00:01:00.217 --> 00:01:01.647
Impulse buying.

17
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.903
Impulse buying means buying something suddenly without planning.

18
00:01:06.517 --> 00:01:09.097
Sweets near the till encourage impulse buying.

19
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:12.881
Your turn. Say: Impulse buying.

20
00:01:15.733 --> 00:01:17.060
Impulse buying.

21
00:01:17.817 --> 00:01:19.247
Price sensitivity.

22
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:24.154
Price sensitivity means how much a change in price affects demand.

23
00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.120
High price sensitivity means shoppers compare carefully.

24
00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:32.124
Your turn. Say: Price sensitivity.

25
00:01:34.967 --> 00:01:36.711
Price sensitivity.

26
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.892
Loyalty program.

27
00:01:39.883 --> 00:01:43.590
Loyalty program means a scheme that rewards repeat customers.

28
00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:47.286
The loyalty program gives points on each purchase.

29
00:01:47.883 --> 00:01:50.756
Your turn. Say: Loyalty program.

30
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.100
Loyalty program.

31
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.072
Social proof.

32
00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:02.324
Social proof means the tendency to follow what other people choose.

33
00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:06.158
Social proof makes popular products more popular.

34
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.611
Your turn. Say: Social proof.

35
00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:14.095
Social proof.

36
00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:16.733
Psychology of pricing.

37
00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.828
Psychology of pricing means how the way prices are shown affects buyers.

38
00:02:22.417 --> 00:02:26.657
The psychology of pricing explains the $9.99 tag.

39
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.436
Your turn. Say: Psychology of pricing.

40
00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.125
Psychology of pricing.

41
00:02:35.883 --> 00:02:36.884
Buying journey.

42
00:02:37.883 --> 00:02:41.590
Buying journey means the steps a customer takes from need to purchase.

43
00:02:42.183 --> 00:02:44.229
The buying journey begins with a search.

44
00:02:44.817 --> 00:02:47.481
Your turn. Say: Buying journey.

45
00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:51.520
Buying journey.

46
00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:56.274
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:57.117 --> 00:03:04.227
Visal, a study says shoppers are 'highly influenced by reviews' and 'strongly attracted to discounts'. Why those adverbs?

48
00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:17.141
Strong collocations: highly influenced, deeply concerned, strongly recommend. Gradable adverbs show how much, and the right pair sounds natural.

49
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.983
Which words do not combine?

50
00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:30.493
We say 'completely satisfied' but not 'very satisfied' with absolute adjectives. And 'highly unlikely', not 'strongly unlikely'.

51
00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:33.873
How does that help describe the buying journey?

52
00:03:34.983 --> 00:03:44.320
Consumers are fairly price-sensitive, extremely influenced by social proof, and occasionally prone to impulse buying.

53
00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:46.886
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:51.247
Grammar focus: Adverb plus adjective collocations.

55
00:03:51.547 --> 00:03:52.757
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.158
Shoppers are highly influenced by reviews.

57
00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:59.909
Many buyers are strongly attracted to discounts.

58
00:04:00.817 --> 00:04:04.302
Customers feel completely satisfied with the loyalty program.

59
00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:16.046
Learn adverb + adjective pairs as chunks: highly influenced, deeply concerned, strongly attracted, completely satisfied. Do not use 'very' with absolute adjectives.

60
00:04:16.783 --> 00:04:21.177
Be careful! Don't say: Shoppers are strongly unlikely to buy.

61
00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:26.178
Say: Shoppers are highly unlikely to buy.

62
00:04:26.478 --> 00:04:28.802
Learn the natural pair: highly unlikely.

63
00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.136
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:32.933 --> 00:04:34.666
Inside the Shopper's Mind.

65
00:04:34.966 --> 00:04:38.788
Marketers study the buying journey to understand every purchase decision.

66
00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:46.014
Shoppers are highly influenced by social proof, and many are strongly attracted to a clear discount.

67
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:53.075
The psychology of pricing explains why a price like $9.99 feels much smaller than $10.

68
00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:59.468
Customers who join a loyalty program often feel completely satisfied and rarely change brand.

69
00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:04.614
Impulse buying, however, shows that emotion can overrule careful thinking.

70
00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:09.562
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:10.417 --> 00:05:12.823
Shoppers are blank influenced by reviews.

72
00:05:13.123 --> 00:05:16.950
A, highly. B, very much of. C, strong.

73
00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.523
The answer is A: highly.

74
00:05:23.683 --> 00:05:26.252
Following what other people choose is blank proof.

75
00:05:26.552 --> 00:05:30.345
A, price. B, social. C, brand.

76
00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.876
The answer is B: social.

77
00:05:37.017 --> 00:05:39.968
Buying something suddenly without planning is blank buying.

78
00:05:40.268 --> 00:05:43.910
A, journey. B, loyalty. C, impulse.

79
00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:49.536
The answer is C: impulse.

80
00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.149
Choose the natural pair.

81
00:05:52.449 --> 00:05:57.252
A, highly unlikely. B, strongly unlikely. C, heavily unlikely.

82
00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:03.368
The answer is A: highly unlikely.

83
00:06:04.517 --> 00:06:08.629
According to the reading, customers in loyalty programs rarely change…

84
00:06:08.929 --> 00:06:12.699
A, brand. B, country. C, language.

85
00:06:16.233 --> 00:06:18.036
The answer is A: brand.

86
00:06:19.233 --> 00:06:22.385
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:27.955
What influences your own purchase decisions the most — price, brand, or reviews?

88
00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:38.181
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:38.481 --> 00:06:59.795
For me, reviews influence my decision the most. I am highly influenced by other customers' honest experiences, because they tell me about quality that a brand cannot. Price also matters, since I am fairly price-sensitive. However, I rarely choose a product just because of its brand name.

90
00:07:00.095 --> 00:07:02.130
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:03.017 --> 00:07:07.933
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and adverb plus adjective collocations.

92
00:07:08.233 --> 00:07:12.476
Today's value is self-awareness. Know your strengths and keep growing.

93
00:07:12.776 --> 00:07:15.440
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:19.182
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

